#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:20
msgid "Pslzme Configuration"
msgstr "pslzme configuration"

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:22
msgid "Pslzme configuration 1"
msgstr "1: Database configuration"

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:24
msgid "explanation 1"
msgstr ""
"To successfully use pslzme a seperate independent database connection is "
"required."

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:25
msgid "explanation 2"
msgstr ""
"To make the configuration as easy as possible for you, you will find a "
"detailed description of the steps required to create and configure the "
"database in the following section."

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:29
msgid "configuration step 1"
msgstr "Step 1: Creation of the database"

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:31
msgid "explanation 3"
msgstr ""
"To create a database, please log in to your chosen server hosting tool and "
"navigate to the Databases section provided. Then select the Create new "
"database option and enter your desired configuration data for the database "
"name, username and password."

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:32
msgid "explanation 4"
msgstr ""
"If you have not yet created a database user, this should ideally be done "
"before the database is created. However, this can also be created later and "
"assigned to the database. To create the user, navigate to the <Create "
"database user> section and then enter the required configuration data such "
"as username and password. Once both the database and the user have been "
"created, the created user must finally be assigned to the database if this "
"has not already been done."

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:38
msgid "configuration step 2"
msgstr "Step 2: Connect database to plszme plugin"

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:39
msgid "explanation 5"
msgstr ""
"Next, please enter the connection data of the database you have just created "
"in the fields below and confirm this by clicking the Save button."

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:47
#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:92
msgid "Save"
msgstr "Save"

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:54
msgid "configuration step 3"
msgstr "Step 3: Configure pslzme tables"

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:55
msgid "explanation 6"
msgstr ""
"Finally, the required pslzme database tables must be created. This is fully "
"automated after clicking the button below. Please check again that the "
"details in the previous step do not contain any errors."

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:58
msgid "tables configured"
msgstr "Tables successfully configured"

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:61
msgid "configure tables"
msgstr "Configure tables"

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:68
msgid "Pslzme configuration 2"
msgstr "2: License domain"

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:70
msgid "explanation 7"
msgstr ""
"Your domain must be licensed in order to use pslzme. First of all, an "
"assigned pslzme account is required. If you do not yet have an account, you "
"can request one at https://www.pslzme.com/en/login. "

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:71
msgid "explanation 8"
msgstr ""
"After your account has been provided, please confirm the following button to "
"license this domain."

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:75
msgid "url licensed"
msgstr "Domain successfully licensed"

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:78
msgid "license domain"
msgstr "Register domain"

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:84
msgid "Pslzme configuration 3"
msgstr "3: Internal page configuration"

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:85
msgid "explanation 9"
msgstr ""
"For a smooth and GDPR-compliant process, pslzme uses internal redirects to "
"certain subpages of your website."

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:86
msgid "explanation 10"
msgstr ""
"For example, the pslzme cookie banner, which functions as an essential "
"component, requires information on the site's legal notice and data "
"protection."

#: admin/partials/pslzme-admin-settings-display.php:87
msgid "explanation 11"
msgstr ""
"To ensure that internal forwarding can be used without any problems, please "
"assign the pages described in the fields below with the corresponding ID to "
"the appropriate internal page. You can find the ID of the respective page in "
"the contao backend under Pages by calling up the detailed information of the "
"respective page."

